<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21248] Add o2ib link state and alias tests using Soft-RoCE</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21248</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;o2iblnd has its own link state handling (kiblnd_handle_link_state_change) and interface alias matching (kiblnd_dev_search), but the sanity-lnet tests for these behaviours (test_214, test_109) only run with tcp NETTYPE.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Soft-RoCE (rdma_rxe) provides an RDMA device on a veth, so o2iblnd can be tested on a tcp node without RDMA hardware.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Add o2ib counterparts of test_214 (NI down/up with the link) and test_109 (NI on an interface alias), using the o2ib interface on o2ib nodes where possible, otherwise Soft-RoCE, and skipping without either.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
